cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or its predictions, please cite it as below.
title: "NanoMatAI: band gaps of 2D semiconductors from crystal structure, with a calibrated trust verdict"
abstract: >-
  A CGCNN ensemble that predicts the band gap of a two-dimensional monolayer from
  its crystal structure on CPU, together with a calibrated uncertainty interval and
  an explicit verdict on whether the prediction is usable. Trained on 22 103 PBE
  monolayers - stable and metastable Alexandria entries and non-magnetic 2DMatPedia
  ones - and evaluated on a composition-disjoint split (MAE 0.225 eV, against 0.430
  for composition alone on the same test set). The graph reads bond angles as well as
  bond lengths, which is what lets it separate polymorphs of one composition. Three
  independent out-of-domain checks decide the verdict: a metal/semiconductor gate, the
  spread between ensemble members, and the distance to the training set in the
  model's own latent space. The 90% interval is calibrated per cell of spread and of
  resemblance to the metastable population, which the latent space detects.
  Linear heads on that same latent space add a quasiparticle gap, an exciton binding
  energy and an absorption onset, and a second ensemble adds the work function, so
  the band edges a contact metal is chosen on follow from the pair. Predictions for
  28 372 public 2D structures are published as a browsable table, and an MCP server
  exposes the tool, verdict first, to language models.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Danil
    family-names: Balandin
    alias: ac1esan
